WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:02.620
This is how a clinic joins LUUMA:

2
00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:06.930
from the first meeting, to
patients supported between visits.

3
00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:11.600
We start by getting to know
how your clinic works:

4
00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:17.160
your clinical system, how many cycles you
run each year, the languages you work in,

5
00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:19.610
and who supports patients between visits.

6
00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:23.920
Then, before anything else, we measure.

7
00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:26.320
Out of every 100 egg retrievals:

8
00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:30.320
how many end in a live birth,
how many are still in treatment,

9
00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:36.100
and how many drop out. We use one definition
for every clinic, and at this stage,

10
00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:38.390
no patient data leaves your clinic.

11
00:00:39.517 --> 00:00:42.947
Next, confidentiality and data protection:

12
00:00:42.997 --> 00:00:47.387
a confidentiality agreement, a
GDPR data processing agreement,

13
00:00:47.437 --> 00:00:50.887
and a clear position on
security and regulation.

14
00:00:50.937 --> 00:00:54.697
All of this is settled before
any patient data is involved.

15
00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:58.940
With that in place, we
send you a proposal.

16
00:00:58.990 --> 00:01:01.920
Once it's accepted, we
plan the pilot together:

17
00:01:01.970 --> 00:01:05.660
how many patients, for how long,
and the outcomes we'll measure:

18
00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:11.750
dropout, quality of life with FertiQoL,
and anxiety and depression with HADS.

19
00:01:13.283 --> 00:01:15.653
Setup takes 2–4 weeks:

20
00:01:15.703 --> 00:01:20.313
we set up your clinic and its care
protocols, add your first physician,

21
00:01:20.363 --> 00:01:23.083
train your team, and run a test patient.

22
00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:26.440
Then it's the patients' turn.

23
00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:30.560
Each patient gets an invitation from
your clinic, gives their consent,

24
00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:32.970
and has a 10-minute welcome conversation.

25
00:01:34.283 --> 00:01:37.373
Patients connect their Fitbit, so sleep,

26
00:01:37.423 --> 00:01:40.393
heart rate and activity
become part of the picture.

27
00:01:40.443 --> 00:01:42.583
And they can disconnect it at any time.

28
00:01:43.683 --> 00:01:47.333
Between visits, patients
do a short daily check-in.

29
00:01:47.383 --> 00:01:51.013
On your side, the team gets an
alert only when it matters.

30
00:01:51.063 --> 00:01:52.623
Less silence between visits.

31
00:01:53.917 --> 00:01:57.167
Measure, support, and measure again.

32
00:01:57.217 --> 00:02:00.837
The goal: less dropout,
against your own baseline.
